abstract: >-
  The Predictive Universe is a theoretical framework exploring how quantum
  behavior, spacetime, and thermodynamics may arise from finite predictive
  systems constrained by self-reference and resources. This research release
  includes the manuscript and appendices, a browser reader with searchable
  text and mathematical notation, 24 interactive conceptual visualizations,
  and the Pure S companion paper with its verification package. The reader
  and visualizations work offline in a modern browser without installation,
  external dependencies, or external fonts.
keywords:
  - predictive systems
  - self-reference
  - theoretical physics
  - quantum emergence
  - spacetime emergence
  - computational complexity
  - interactive visualization
license: MIT
